SUMMARY:Land and Harvest Festival
DESCRIPTION:Join TLC for our 2nd annual Land and Harvest Festival!\nHelp us gather at our Williamson Farm and Nature Preserve to celebrate local agriculture\, support Williamson farmers\, and connect over shared values of land conservation\, sustainability\, and food systems. As we celebrate\, we will host a tour of the historic buildings on the property\, explore nearby groves of Chickasaw plum\, and enjoy live Bluegrass music\, food trucks\, and fun activities!\n\nA key highlight of the festival will be the Farmers and Vendor Market\, where you can purchase fresh\, locally grown produce and support local vendors. In addition\, we’ll be spotlighting the Williamson Farm Program\, which plays a crucial role in supporting farmers\, preserving open spaces\, and contributing to the local food system in Eastern Wake and Johnston Counties. Throughout the event\, you'll have the opportunity to meet local organizations showcasing their work dedicated to sustainable food practices and environmental conservation. This is a free event but preregistration is required.\n\n\nFarmers and Vendors:\n\n 	Karen Community Farm\n 	Urban Community AgriNomics\n 	Reclamation Farmacy\n 	Footprints in the Garden\n 	Poetry Fox\n\nFood Vendors:\n\n 	Karen Community Farm\n 	Copperhead’s Craft Burgers\n 	Lumpy’s Ice Cream\n 	Crankarm Brewing\n\nEvent Schedule:\nAll day:\n\n 	Adaptive Cycling with NC Adapted Sports\n 	Kid's Corner!\n 	Birding with Feminist Bird Club (Various times)\n\nMusic:\n\n 	Bluegrass Jam Group\n\n 	1-1:45 pm\n 	2:30-3:15 pm\n\n\n\nHikes:\n\n 	Chickasaw Plum Hike (1:30-2:30pm)\n 	Tour of Williamson Historic Buildings (2:30pm)\n 	Karen Community Farm Tour (3:00pm) 
URL:https://triangleland.org/event/land-and-harvest-festival
LOCATION:Williamson Nature Preserve [Staff Entrance]\, 4429 Old Country Mial Rd\, Raleigh\, NC\, 27610\, United States
ORGANIZER;CN="Amaya Horner":MAILTO:ahorner@triangleland.org
END:VEVENT
