SUMMARY:Trail Talks with TLC: Brumley North
DESCRIPTION:Get a special look at TLC's work on this staff led hike series!\nJoin TLC Grants Manager\, Laura Warman\, and Working Lands Manager\, Emma Childs\, on an exploration of Brumley North Nature Preserve. Learn about the forest ecology within the various habitats of Brumley that have made this preserve a popular spot for birders\, hikers\, bikers\, and naturalists! This is a free event\, but preregistration is required.\n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n\n\n \n\nInclement Weather Policy: In the event of inclement weather\, you will be contacted by email for a call on cancellation or postponement.\n\nCurrent Mask Policy: TLC seeks to build a supportive\, mask-friendly environment in all collaborations with staff and the public. Please wear a mask if you are not vaccinated\, or if that makes you feel most comfortable. We also encourage those eligible to be vaccinated to get their Covid-19 vaccine and booster shot. If you are experiencing any Covid-related symptoms\, please stay home and attend a program another day. Our top priority is to create a safe environment for our community. Thank you for your understanding.\n\n 
URL:https://triangleland.org/event/trail-talks-with-tlc-brumley
LOCATION:Brumley North Nature Preserve\, 3620 Old State Highway 10\, Chapel Hill\, NC\, 27514\, United States
ORGANIZER;CN="Amaya Horner":MAILTO:ahorner@triangleland.org
END:VEVENT
